WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Speaker 1: Hello, everyone. Welcome to The David&nbsp;
Pakman Show. I'm producer Pat Forde, filling in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.640
for David today as he continues his paternity&nbsp;
leave. David should be making his triumphant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.840
return to the show soon, relatively soon. But&nbsp;
he's, of course, taking this time to enjoy himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.680
as a new parent and to spend some time with the&nbsp;
little one and get some sleep whenever he can find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.440
the time to. Today, we're gonna be talking about&nbsp;
a number of different topics. We're going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.920
talking about the January 6th hearings. We're&nbsp;
going to talk about inflation and gas prices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.320
and all these different things. But I wanted to&nbsp;
start today talking about gun control, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:38.640
there's a new bipartisan deal in the Senate on&nbsp;
the topic of gun control, and it actually includes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.360
ten Republican senators, which is crucial because&nbsp;
that means there's a solid chance of this actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.600
passing in the coming weeks and becoming&nbsp;
law. I don't want to celebrate it too much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.720
because for one, it hasn't actually happened yet.&nbsp;
Right. And these things could fall through. We we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.080
need to see the actual text, but also it&nbsp;
seems a little bit lackluster. It doesn't come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.320
nearly close to all the things that we have to&nbsp;
do to actually make a difference when it comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:08.320
guns and gun safety in this country. But given&nbsp;
the fact that Republicans have been steadfast in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.760
their refusal to do anything about guns in&nbsp;
the wake of mass shootings over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:20.240
it's hard to not feel some level of optimism over&nbsp;
this announced agreement. The deal will include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:26.000
support for state crisis intervention orders,&nbsp;
funding for school safety resources, an enhanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:32.160
review process for buyers of guns under the age of&nbsp;
21, and penalties for straw purchases. That's when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.360
you have one person purchase a weapon on someone&nbsp;
else's behalf. The legislation will also have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:42.240
red flag provision so that states and courts will&nbsp;
have the resources to make sure firearms are kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.360
out of the hands of people who are at significant&nbsp;
risk of doing harm with them. There's also going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:53.360
to be increased funding for mental health, suicide&nbsp;
prevention and trauma intervention, which is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.440
of course, an important aspect to all of this. We&nbsp;
know that the right wing in this country loves to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.480
claim that mass shootings are all about mental&nbsp;
health and that they're just exclusively a mental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.880
health issue. We know that they just use it as&nbsp;
a red herring. But there's there's something to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.600
that, right? Because that is one aspect in all of&nbsp;
this. And we have to not only look at gun control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.960
measures, we have to look at the mental health&nbsp;
side as well. So if they're willing to have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.000
good faith conversation about mental health, we&nbsp;
should absolutely take them up on that and take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.280
advantage of it. The ten Republican senators who&nbsp;
have signed on to this piece of legislation that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:32.400
in the works are John Cornyn, Thom Tillis, Richard&nbsp;
Burr, Roy Blunt, Bill Cassidy, Susan Collins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:39.920
Lindsey Graham, Rob Portman, Mitt Romney and Pat&nbsp;
Toomey. The centrist Democrats who tend to torpedo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:45.520
pieces of legislation that we like as progressives&nbsp;
and Democrats. Those are Joe Manchin and Kirsten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.320
Cinema. They've also pledged their support. So&nbsp;
this is very, very promising. Joe Biden said about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.520
this, quote, Obviously, it does not do everything&nbsp;
that I think is needed, but it reflects important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:01.200
steps in the right direction and would make the&nbsp;
most significant gun safety legislation to pass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:08.000
Congress in decades. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez&nbsp;
said about the bill. If we get a real baby step,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:14.320
not kind of a distraction from the solution, she's&nbsp;
going to support it. So both Biden and AOC kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.720
providing the same sentiment there that like,&nbsp;
yeah, this is great and all, but we could just do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:24.640
so much more if we had more willingness from the&nbsp;
Republicans to do anything about guns. Sadly, I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.880
think this is going to be treated as the solution.&nbsp;
That's probably what we'll see. We'll probably see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.680
this get signed into law and then they'll do some&nbsp;
sort of victory lap and everyone will pretend as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.720
if we actually did something significant when it&nbsp;
comes to gun safety in this country, when we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.080
we can just go so much further. You know, there&nbsp;
are some solid provisions in this legislation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:49.120
that's for sure. But we know that we can do more&nbsp;
when it comes to universal background checks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:55.040
raising the legal age to own a semiautomatic&nbsp;
rifle to 21 magazine capacity limits. None of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:00.560
stuff's in there. So maybe we can try with future&nbsp;
legislation, but it just doesn't seem like it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:06.480
going to be able to happen any time soon. For as&nbsp;
long as we have such a slim majority in Congress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.880
and for as long as Republicans are not willing to&nbsp;
compromise on much when it comes to this issue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:16.240
So definitely go ahead, pass the bill. Let's try&nbsp;
to avoid the victory laps afterwards. I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:23.520
see us try to make this a voting issue come the&nbsp;
2022 midterms, because it seems like now we do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:28.240
have somewhat of a chance of maybe holding on to&nbsp;
the House and Senate. It would be great to to pick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.040
up an extra two Senate seats, because that means&nbsp;
that we could potentially eliminate the filibuster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:38.560
and do so much more. And I think, you know, this&nbsp;
focus on abortion and gun control at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.360
given how the economy is, might have to be the&nbsp;
path forward for Democrats. The kitchen table&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:49.520
issues tend to be more economic and financial&nbsp;
issues. And there's some aspects of that that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.040
you know, we're having a tough time communicating&nbsp;
about because gas prices are so high,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:00.160
inflation so high. So maybe given this a. Courts&nbsp;
leak draft opinion when it comes to abortion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:06.000
Maybe, you know, the mass shootings and the&nbsp;
backing for new gun control measures, that's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.800
to be enough to maybe propel Democrats to hold&nbsp;
on to the majorities. But we just don't know yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.880
and we really don't know what the big issues are&nbsp;
going to have to be once it's actually time to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.920
vote. So that's the latest when it comes to gun&nbsp;
control. It looks like we're going to have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.640
piece of legislation pass through the Senate&nbsp;
and the House, and that's very good to see.

